# prebuilds/win32-x64

Node tag: `win32` + `x64` (Windows x86_64).
Typical EPICS copy source: `windows-x64` (`bin` / `lib`).

## Build environment (fill in when packaging)

- OS
- MSVC / Node.js
- EPICS base: 7.0.10
- pvxs: 1.5.2
- libevent: 2.1

## Files to copy here

From `npm run build`:

- `./build/Release/pvxs.node`

From your EPICS / pvxs / libevent install (names may vary slightly):

- `pvxs.dll`
- `Com.dll`
- `event_core.dll`

No RPATH rewrite is required on Windows. At runtime, `lib/binding.js` loads `pvxs.node` **only** from this directory and adds it to `PATH` / `addDllDirectory`.

## Self-test

From the package root (after copying files above; no extra `PATH` setup needed):

```bash
node -e "console.log(require('.').version())"
```
